 * Glyph — one parkour movement glyph, rendered as inline, individually
 * animatable SVG path segments.
 *
 * Ported from src/stories/Brand/Glyph/glyphs.js (`PARKOUR_GLYPHS`, `glyphSvg()`).
 * A 16-glyph slice of the full 67-mark set (grids2601/app/src/data/parkour-glyphs.ts) —
 * one per distinct motion verb. Each glyph is viewBox 0 0 240 240, drawn as
 * filled <path> segments in currentColor.
 *
 * Render contract for the motion layer (Animation/Brand/GlyphAssembly), and
 * why this MUST stay inline paths rather than lp_icon()/the sprite: the
 * glyph-assembly effect reads and animates the individual <path> DOM nodes
 * directly. A `<use>` reference to the #glyph-icons sprite (the other,
 * static 67-mark set, used everywhere a glyph does NOT need to animate) is a
 * black box the effect cannot reach into. This boundary was settled
 * 2026-08-01 in the Storybook and is not to be reconciled — extend this array
 * only when a mark needs glyph-assembly animation; a new static mark belongs
 * in the sprite, not here. bin/audit-reuse.sh exempts parts/brand/ from the
 * "no raw <svg>" rule for exactly this reason.
 *
 * Every data-motion-* attribute is carried over verbatim: data-motion-scope
 * on the <svg>, data-motion-verb from each glyph's own `motion` key, and
 * data-motion-element="segment" on every <path>.
 *
 * Deliberate departure: the source's `glyphSvg()` throws on an unknown
 * glyphId. This partial has no exception mechanism to throw into, so an
 * unknown glyph_id renders nothing (same "return early" convention as
 * parts/elements/button.php and parts/elements/glyph-label.php).
 *
 * label/description are not part of the render contract (glyphSvg() never
 * reads them) and are not ported here — they belong to a future glyph
 * catalog listing, not this render.
 *
 * @param string $args['glyph_id']  Key into the glyph set below, e.g. 'vaulting'.
 * @param string $args['class_name'] Extra classes on the <svg>, e.g. 'text-primary'.
 * @param string $args['label']     Accessible label; omit for decorative (aria-hidden).
 *
 * @package londonparkour_v8
 */

